\caption{Test 14: asymmetric warp with variable scale height, central shift and shift in systemic velocity. Noise added to the data cube. The cloud flux used was $10^{-3}\,{\rm Jy}\,{\rm km}\,{\rm s}^{-1}$ for a radius below $48\arcsec$, $10^{-4}\,{\rm Jy}\,{\rm km}\,{\rm s}^{-1}$ for a radius between $48\arcsec$ and $114\arcsec$, and $10^{-4}\,{\rm Jy}\,{\rm km}\,{\rm s}^{-1}$ beyond $114\arcsec$, correspinding to \ion{H}{i} masses of $3.8\cdot 10^4\,{\rm M}_\odot$, $3.8\cdot 10^3\,{\rm M}_\odot$, and $3.8\cdot 10^2\,{\rm M}_\odot$, respectively, for a galaxy at a distance of $4\,{\rm Mpc}$, the cloud masses scaling with the distance squared. With this setup, an inhomogeneous distibution of the \ion{H}{i} was simulated. Since the orientation of the galactic disk is near to edge-on, no attempt was made to perform a fit to the velocity field. \scc}
